Students are expected to know and be able to:

1. understand the role of gender in China from past to present, and how gender was interwoven with social, cultural, economic and political forces;
2. analyse gender related elements that are reflected from sources, methodologies and discourses;
3. evaluate existing values and perceptions about gender issues in China and increase gender awareness.

Upon successful completion of this course, students will be able to:
1. State the key issues and debates in contemporary gender studies and feminist scholarship;
2. Understand difficult founding texts of feminisms and gender studies;
3. Describe different perspectives within feminisms and gender studies;
4. Compare and contrast various perspectives with sound justifications;
5. Theorize cultural issues from gender perspectives.

Upon successful completion of this course, students will be able to:

1. Understand questions of violence and women in contemporary times and the effectiveness of ways in which violence is negotiated;
2. Gain knowledge of different theories and concepts on peace and everyday life;
3. Re-examine practices for peace from a feminist perspective in their personal and social milieu.

